{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTypeAInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTypeAInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Matrix"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeA_jmRaw_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeA_jmRaw_succ","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L161-L166","doc":"The multiplicative Jucys–Murphy recursion `L_{i+1} = σᵢ Lᵢ σᵢ` in the type-A Hecke\nalgebra, with `σ` the genuine rescaled generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeA_jmRaw_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeA_jmRaw_comm","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L155-L159","doc":"Jucys–Murphy elements commute **in the type-A Hecke algebra**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.instNontrivialTypeAHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.instNontrivialTypeAHecke","kind":"instance","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L141-L147","doc":"**The type-A Hecke algebra does not collapse.**\n\nWithout this the `HeckeGenerators` instance below would be inhabited but vacuous — every\ntheorem the arc transports would hold of the zero ring. The witness is the index\nrepresentation `T_i ↦ q²`, which exists because `typeAMatrix` is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAHeckeGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAHeckeGenerators","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L112-L139","doc":"**The unbounded `HeckeGenerators` instance on the actual type-A Hecke algebra.**\n\n`σ i = q⁻¹ · T i` is the convention bridge; the inverse is read straight off the Hecke\nrelation, since `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1` says exactly that `σ − (q − q⁻¹)` is a two-sided\ninverse of `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT_far","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L102-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT_braid","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L95-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L91-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAT","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The Iwahori-normalised generators of the type-A Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.TypeAHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.TypeAHecke","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L83-L86","doc":"**The type-A Iwahori–Hecke algebra** at corpus parameter `q`, built at the Iwahori\nparameter `Q = q²` so that the rescaled generators land in the corpus convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_symm","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L75-L79","doc":"The type-A matrix is symmetric — needed for the non-vacuity witness below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_eq_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_eq_An","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L62-L73","doc":"**Agreement with Mathlib's `CoxeterMatrix.Aₙ`.** On the common range the ℕ-indexed\nmatrix above *is* Mathlib's type-A Coxeter matrix.\n\nMathlib does have `Aₙ : (n : ℕ) → CoxeterMatrix (Fin n)`; the reason this file does not\nsimply use it is the indexing. `Aₙ N` is `Fin N`-indexed, which pins one `n`, whereas\nthe `HeckeGenerators` class is ℕ-indexed and unbounded. Stating the agreement keeps the\ntwo from being merely parallel: anything proved about `Aₙ` transfers here on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_of_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_of_gt","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L57-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L52-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_succ_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_succ_left","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L49-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_succ_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix_succ_right","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L46-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAMatrix","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTypeAInstance.lean#L36-L44","doc":"The Coxeter matrix of type `A_∞`, on the index set `ℕ` of strand positions:\nadjacent generators braid (`m = 3`), non-adjacent ones commute (`m = 2`), and the\ndiagonal is `1`.\n\nIndexing by `ℕ` rather than `Fin (n-1)` is deliberate. The relations then hold at every\nindex, so this single object serves every `n` at once: `HeckeGenerators` (unbounded) is\ninhabited, and each `HeckeGeneratorsBelow n` follows by restriction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}